        "original_id": "24deadf0-2743-58b5-826b-5858c259ce63",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Great Santini\n- People: Lewis John Carlino, Pat Conroy, Michael O'Keefe\n- Concepts: tragic hero\n- Roles: Ben Meechum, Danny Noonan\n- Awards: Golden Globe Award for New Star of the Year, Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor\n\nFacts:\n- Pat Conroy wrote the 1976 novel The Great Santini.\n- The Great Santini is a 1979 American drama film written and directed by Lewis John Carlino and based on Pat Conroy's 1976 novel of the same name.\n- Michael O'Keefe was born Raymond Peter O'Keefe, Jr. on April 24, 1955, and he is an American film and television actor.\n- Michael O'Keefe played Ben Meechum in The Great Santini.\n- Michael O'Keefe received a Golden Globe Award for New Star of the Year and an Academy Award nomination for Best Supporting Actor for The Great Santini.\n- Michael O'Keefe is also known for playing Danny Noonan in Caddyshack.\n- A tragic hero is the protagonist of a tragedy in drama.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
